---
title: Baked Mac and Cheese (CSO)
description: A decadently rich version you'd expect from a cheese-loving Wisconsin company.
course: side dishes
difficulty: medium
cook time: 60 minutes
servings: 10
source.author: Sub-Zero Wolf, Mastering the CSO
source.url: https://www.subzero-wolf.com/
tags: CSO, steam
---

= Pasta =

Place @elbow pasta{1%lb}(dry) in a large, shallow, oven-save dish. 
Add just enough @water to barely cover the pasta.

Position the wire rack in the middle position of the #Convection Steam Oven{} (CSO).
Place the dish on the rack and set the oven to 340°F on Convection Steam mode.

Cook for ~{20%min} or until pasta is al dente. 
Remove the dish from the oven and strain any excess water.
Let pasta cool.

Change the oven setting to 375°F on Convection Steam mode.

= Sauce =

While the pasta cooks, in a #large saucepan{} over medium heat, melt @butter{1%tbsp}.
Add @all-purpose flour{2%tbsp} and whisk to combine into a paste. 
Cook for ~{1-2%min}, whisking continuously.

Slowly add @whole milk{1/2%cup}, whisking until well combined.
Slowly add remaining @whole milk{3.25%cups}, whisking continuously.
Bring the milk to a simmer, frequently stirring and scraping the bottom of the pan to prefvent scorching.

Add @salt{1.5%tsp}, @onion powder{1/4%tsp}, @ground mustard{1/8%tsp},
@garlic powder{1/8%tsp}, and @smoked paprika{1/8%tsp}.
Let simmer ~{20%min}.

Remove the pan from the heat and add @smoked gouda{3/4%cup}(shredded), 
@American cheese{1/2%cup}(diced), @sharp cheddar cheese{1%cup}(shredded),
and @Parmesan cheese{1/4%cup}(shredded).
Stir until fully melted.

Add cooked pasta to the sauce and stir to combine.
Pour the pasta mixture into a #large casserole dish{}.

= Finishing =

In a medium bowl, combine @sharp cheddar cheese{1%cup}(shredded) and @breadcrumbs{1%cup}.

After the oven has finished preheating to 375°F, sprinkle the breadcrumbs over the pasta.

Bake the dish until the top begins to brown, ~{10-15%min}.
